I have gathered a complete picture of the membership tier feature. Here is my report.

## Summary

The membership tier is a **derived/computed value** produced at DTO-mapping time (not stored on the entity). The current rule only returns `SILVER` or `BRONZE`. The acceptance test expects a `GOLD` tier that is **not yet implemented**.

---

## 1. Membership tier logic (BRONZE/SILVER rule)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** (MapStruct interface)

The tier is wired into `toOwnerDto` via an expression mapping (line 25) and computed by the `membershipTier` default method (lines 43-51):

```java
@Mapping(target = "membershipTier", expression = "java(membershipTier(owner))")
OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);
...
/**
 * The owner's membership tier: 'SILVER' when namesakeCount is 0 and an email
 * address is present, otherwise 'BRONZE'.
 */
default String membershipTier(Owner owner) {
    boolean uniqueName = owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0;
    boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank();
    return uniqueName && hasEmail ? "SILVER" : "BRONZE";
}
```

Notes:
- There is **no GOLD branch** here today. The `GOLD` string appears only in the acceptance test (expectation).
- `membershipTier` is a field on the generated `OwnerDto` (an OpenAPI-generated DTO); the `Owner` entity itself has no `membershipTier` field/column.

---

## 2. Owner entity and `householdId`

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`**

JPA entity `@Entity @Table(name = "owners")`, extends `Person`. `householdId` is defined at lines 62-63 with getter/setter at lines 125-131:

```java
@Column(name = "household_id")
private String householdId;
```

Other tier-relevant fields on the entity: `email` (52-54), `registrationDate` (56-57), `customerCode` (59-60), `namesakeCount` (65-66), `membershipNumber` (68-69), `bulkSignupWarning` (71-72). There is no `membershipTier` field.

---

## 3. The create logic (where the owner is built and saved)

Important: the "create + set fields" logic lives in the **REST controller**, not in the service. The service `saveOwner` is a thin passthrough.

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** — `addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` starts at line 128. Key portion (lines 176-201) where household/namesake/membership are set:

```java
String lastNameKey = normalizeIdentity(owner.getLastName());
String addressKey = addressNormalizer.normalize(owner.getAddress());
if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold())) {
    boolean householdDuplicate = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
        .anyMatch(existing -> normalizeIdentity(existing.getLastName()).equals(lastNameKey)
            && addressNormalizer.normalize(existing.getAddress()).equals(addressKey));
    if (householdDuplicate) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
    }
}
owner.setHouseholdId(householdId(lastNameKey, addressKey));
owner.setCustomerCode(nextCustomerCode(owner.getCity(), owner.getLastName()));
int namesakeCount = (int) this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
    .filter(existing -> owner.getFirstName().equalsIgnoreCase(existing.getFirstName())
        && owner.getLastName().equalsIgnoreCase(existing.getLastName()))
    .count();
owner.setNamesakeCount(namesakeCount);
owner.setMembershipNumber(membershipNumber(owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate()));
owner.setBulkSignupWarning(ownersCreatedThatDay > 80);
this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
...
OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);   // tier computed here
