## 5. Tests related to membership tier / owner creation

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`** — the only test that asserts on `membershipTier`. It expects **GOLD** for a 3+ member household (a rule not yet implemented in `OwnerMapper`):

```java
/** tier-gold: membershipTier is 'GOLD' when the owner's household has 3+ members after this
 * create. ... */
@Test
void coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold() throws Exception {
    String lastName = uniqueLastName();
    String address = uniqueAddress();
    for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
        ObjectNode m = ownerNode();
        m.put("lastName", lastName);
        m.put("address", address);
        m.put("sharesHousehold", true);
        createOwnerOk(m);
    }
    ObjectNode third = ownerNode();
    third.put("lastName", lastName);
    third.put("address", address);
    third.put("sharesHousehold", true);
    int id = createOwnerOk(third);
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.membershipTier").value("GOLD"));
}
```

Supporting test infrastructure (black-box, hits `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`):
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** — base class (`@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, `@Transactional`, `@WithMockUser`). Provides `ownerNode()`, `createOwnerOk()`, `getOwner()`, unique-data generators, and replicated algorithms (`sha256hex`, `shaHex`, `luhn`). Note: each test is transactional/rolled back, so counts see only seed data plus what the test creates.
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java`** — audit log test helper.

No dedicated unit test for `OwnerMapper.membershipTier` exists.

---

## 6. Build tool and running tests

Build tool: **Maven** (there is a `pom.xml` and Maven wrapper `mvnw`/`mvnw.cmd`; no Gradle files).

Run the full suite from `/home/daniel/sandbox`:
- `./mvnw test` — run unit/integration tests
- `./mvnw verify` — full build incl. tests
- Single test class: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`
- Single method: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest#coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold`

There is also a `docker-compose.yml` and `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root you may want to consult for run/profile details.

---

## Key takeaway for the feature

To implement the expected GOLD tier, the change point is `OwnerMapper.membershipTier(Owner)` in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`. However, that method currently only has access to a single `Owner` (namesakeCount + email) — it has **no household member count**. Determining "household has 3+ members" requires counting owners sharing the same `householdId` (set during create in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`), which the mapper cannot currently see. So implementing GOLD will likely require passing household size into the mapper or computing/storing it during create.

